<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Changshan</h1><p class="st-meta">206 BCE – 205 BCE · capital Xiangguo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Zhang Er's kingdom in Hebei, carved from Zhao by Xiang Yu in 206 BCE, which fell to his former friend Chen Yu within a year.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-er">Zhang Er</a> had been chancellor of the revived state of Zhao during the rebellion against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a>. In 206 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> made him King of Changshan, ruling most of Zhao from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xingtai">Xiangguo</a> (near Xingtai), while the Zhao king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-xie">Zhao Xie</a> was moved north to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dai-206-bc">Kingdom of Dai</a> (206 BC).</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom was dominated by the bitter quarrel between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-er">Zhang Er</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-yu">Chen Yu</a>, once sworn friends, who had fallen out during the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-julu">Julu</a>. Chen Yu, given only a few counties, felt cheated by the settlement.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 205 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chen-yu">Chen Yu</a>, with troops from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-rong">Tian Rong</a> of Qi (206 BC), drove <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-er">Zhang Er</a> out; Zhang fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-xie">Zhao Xie</a> was restored as King of Zhao. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-xin">Han Xin</a> defeated Zhao at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jingxing">Jingxing</a> in 204 BCE, Liu Bang made Zhang Er King of Zhao.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 206 BCE – 205 BCE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:55.60%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>206 BCE – 205 BCE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Xiangguo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zhang Er</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Chinese ancestral religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Chinese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>China</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Changshan (Zhang Er)</dd></dl></aside></div>

